[rvn-ple] Refuse NEXTN on an RVN text checkpoint that ships no draft layer

rvn-w4a16 only: the gate fires when the config is an RVN text model
(architectures=Qwen4ExpForCausalLM and model_type=qwen4_exp_text), the
speculative algorithm is NEXTN (resolved to EAGLE) and no
--speculative-draft-model-path was given. The LIL multimodal
(Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration) path and every external-draft launch take
the same return-None branch as before, and no other architecture is named.

The NEXTN dry run died in the draft worker with CUDA out of memory while it
allocated the n-gram table as a 47.68 GiB VocabParallelEmbedding on the device.
That table belongs to a second, full copy of the model: the draft arch remap in
configs/model_config.py:747 is keyed on the multimodal arch only, so an RVN text
draft worker builds the target model again -- and because patch 0051 propagates
ple_offload_embedding only for not is_draft_worker
(model_runner_components/load_model_utils.py:281), this copy allocates the
n-gram table on the device instead of pinning it on the host.

There is nothing for that draft to be. RVN text is defined as MTP-free:
normalize_text_config pins mtp_num_hidden_layers to 0,
Qwen4ExpForCausalLM asserts rvn_mtp_count(config) == 0 at construction
(models/qwen4_exp.py:3060), and its loader sends every name through
reject_non_text_weight_name, which rejects model.mtp.* -- as the working target
launch proves, since it loads 296,238 tensors with none named model.mtp.*. So
refuse the combination at argument resolution, before any allocation, with the
reason and the two ways out.

Why the alternatives are wrong, not merely bigger:
  * Propagating ple_offload_embedding to the draft worker would pin a second
    26.8 GiB host copy of a table the draft never reads: the upstream MTP draft
    clears config.ple_layer_ids (models/qwen4_exp_mtp.py:46) so
    _init_qwen4_exp_layer_extensions leaves self.ple = None. It would also
    still leave a 48-layer duplicate of the target in the draft worker.
  * Remapping the RVN text draft arch to Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP, the way the
    multimodal arch is remapped, would remove the allocation but load a draft
    with nothing to load: it inherits Qwen3_5ForCausalLMMTP.load_weights, the
    checkpoint carries no model.mtp.* tensors, so it would construct, "load" and
    serve an untrained head -- a false pass against the acceptance line, worse
    than a clear refusal.

The two arch gaps stay gaps for the day an RVN checkpoint does ship MTP layers:
configs/model_config.py:747 (draft arch remap) and the list at
arg_groups/speculative_hook.py:580-597 that defaults the draft path to the target
path. Neither is reachable until the 0047 text contract permits model.mtp.*
names, so neither is patched here.

Regression: tests/rvn_ple/test_rvn_nextn_draft_gate.py is red on the preimage
(the predicate does not exist, and the launch reaches the allocation) and green
with this patch, including the negative cases that keep LIL, STANDALONE and
external-draft launches out of the gate.

--- a/python/sglang/srt/arg_groups/speculative_hook.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/arg_groups/speculative_hook.py
@@ -540,6 +540,52 @@
         )
 
 
+def rvn_text_bundled_draft_unsupported(
+    algorithm: Optional[str],
+    config: object,
+    draft_model_path: Optional[str],
+) -> Optional[str]:
+    """Why an RVN text checkpoint cannot host a bundled NEXTN draft layer.
+
+    Returns the reason to reject the launch, or None when it is fine. The RVN
+    text contract pins ``mtp_num_hidden_layers`` to 0
+    (models/qwen4_exp_text_adapter.py:normalize_text_config), the
+    ``Qwen4ExpForCausalLM`` entry class asserts that count at construction, and
+    its loader rejects ``model.mtp.*`` tensor names outright -- the shipped
+    candidate index carries none of them (296,238 tensors, zero matches). There
+    is therefore no draft layer to build.
+
+    Without this check the launch does not fail cleanly: the draft worker's
+    architecture is never remapped to ``Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP`` (that remap in
+    configs/model_config.py is keyed on the multimodal arch alone), so the
+    draft worker constructs the *target* model a second time -- and because
+    patch 0051 propagates ``ple_offload_embedding`` only for
+    ``not is_draft_worker``, the draft's n-gram table is allocated eagerly on
+    the device as a 47.68 GiB ``VocabParallelEmbedding`` and OOMs the load.
+    """
+    from sglang.srt.models.qwen4_exp_text_adapter import (
+        is_rvn_text_config,
+        rvn_mtp_count,
+    )
+
+    # "EAGLE" is what --speculative-algorithm NEXTN resolves to by now
+    # (_resolve_speculative_algorithm_alias), and no draft path means the draft
+    # layer is expected inside this checkpoint. STANDALONE and an explicit
+    # --speculative-draft-model-path bring their own weights and stay untouched.
+    if algorithm != "EAGLE" or draft_model_path is not None:
+        return None
+    if not is_rvn_text_config(config) or rvn_mtp_count(config) > 0:
+        return None
+    return (
+        "--speculative-algorithm NEXTN builds its draft layer from the target "
+        "checkpoint (model.mtp.*), but this RVN text checkpoint declares no MTP "
+        f"layers (mtp_num_hidden_layers + num_nextn_predict_layers = "
+        f"{rvn_mtp_count(config)}) and its text loader rejects model.mtp.* "
+        "weights, so no draft exists. Serve without speculative decoding, or "
+        "point --speculative-draft-model-path at an external draft checkpoint."
+    )
+
+
 def _handle_eagle_family(server_args: ServerArgs) -> None:
     from sglang.srt.arg_groups.overrides import (
         attention_backends_of,
@@ -576,7 +622,19 @@
             "eagle speculative decoding."
         )
 
-    model_arch = server_args.get_model_config().hf_config.architectures[0]
+    hf_config = server_args.get_model_config().hf_config
+    model_arch = hf_config.architectures[0]
+    # The candidate that ships no draft layer must be refused here: further
+    # down, the draft worker would build the whole target model a second time
+    # and OOM on the n-gram table (see rvn_text_bundled_draft_unsupported).
+    bundled_draft_unsupported = rvn_text_bundled_draft_unsupported(
+        server_args.speculative_algorithm,
+        hf_config,
+        server_args.speculative_draft_model_path,
+    )
+    if bundled_draft_unsupported:
+        raise ValueError(bundled_draft_unsupported)
+
     if model_arch in [
         "DeepseekV32ForCausalLM",
         "DeepseekV3ForCausalLM",
